       }
      ],
      "text": "Role in ADHD:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " preschoolers: behavioral therapy first; meds if the response is inadequate or Sx are moderate–severe; school-aged children: behavioral therapy + medication; methylphenidate or amphetamine salts are the most widely used."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Common AEs: insomnia, HA, stomachache, appetite suppression, ↑HR and BP; height growth slows over 2 yrs of use, and adult height potential may be ↓ w chronic use."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
